      "pos": [
        54,
        1
      ],
      "data": {
        "text": "A shape is cabled round a loop: the Video Mixer feeds the Rotator, the Rotator feeds the Frame Delay, and the Frame Delay comes back into the mixer's second input. Without the delay this loop would be an error. With it, every picture is built from the last one, three frames old, turned and shrunk a little, so the shape leaves a spiralling trail.\nTwo slow LFOs walk the shape around, so the trail keeps changing.\nTry FRAMES on the Frame Delay: longer makes a wider, more broken trail.\nTry the Video Mixer FADER: higher keeps the trail longer, and near the top it fills the picture. Try ANGLE and ZOOM on the Rotator.\nThe Display shows the mixer. A second Display on the Frame Delay would show the same trail, three frames late."
      }
    }
  ],
